# Ordered shared SDM845 patches, one path per line.
#
# Empty on purpose. No XNU patch is known to be required by the SoC itself yet;
# the two candidates are still unimplemented and are recorded in the device
# repository's patches/xnu/series instead:
#
#   - no PAuth: SDM845's A75/A55 are ARMv8.2, the OS profile targets arm64 with
#     no FEAT_PAuth, so nothing should need patching. Confirm at P5.
#   - apps SMMU is a qcom,qsmmu-v500 and XNU's ArmSmmu4K has no V500 path. That
#     patch, when it exists, is SoC work and belongs here.
#
# scripts/unixnu/patches.py rejects a missing file and a duplicated entry, and
# applies them in this order; a bare filename is relative to this directory.

# The ApplePMGR bridge, byte-identical to UniXNU's patches/xnu copy and to the
# SM8550 SoC layer's.  It is not optional: the OS series patch
# patches/xnu/zzz-boot-progress.patch inserts boot_progress_stage() calls into
# the "#if defined(XNU_SHENG_PMGR)" block that this patch adds to bsd_init.c,
# so leaving it out makes the OS series fail with
#   error: patch failed: bsd/kern/bsd_init.c:773
# The block is compiled out unless CONFIG_XNU_SHENG_PMGR is set, so carrying
# the patch without the matching archive is safe for a console-only first boot.
sheng-platform-power.patch
